---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'

const link = 'link'
---
<Base
  title="AudioSilo - Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for the AudioSilo self-hosted audiobook player."
>
  <div class="shell py-14 sm:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-[1.0625rem]">
      <h1 class="t-display">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 mb-10 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Last updated: 25 June 2026</p>

      <p class="t-lede mb-6 text-foreground/80">
        AudioSilo is a <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">self-hosted audiobook player</strong>. The AudioSilo
        app is a <em>client</em> for an AudioSilo server that <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">you</strong>
        (or whoever administers your server) run and control. In normal use, the app communicates
        <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">only</strong> with the server address you provide, and the developer
        of AudioSilo operates
        <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">no service that receives, stores, or processes your data</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-14 mb-4 font-display text-[1.625rem] font-bold tracking-[-0.03em]">Who we are</h2>
      <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-foreground/85">
        AudioSilo ("the app") is published by <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">KodeStar</strong>. Questions
        about this policy can be sent to
        <a class={link} href="mailto:kode@audiosilo.app">kode@audiosilo.app</a>.
      </p>

      <div class="my-10 rounded-3xl bg-muted/70 p-6 shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--border)] sm:p-8">
        <p class="mt-6 mb-2 font-semibold text-foreground">The short version</p>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 marker:text-subtle-foreground">
          <li>We do <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">not</strong> collect, see, sell, or share your personal data.</li>
          <li>
            We use <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">no</strong> analytics, advertising, tracking, or
            crash-reporting services.
          </li>
          <li>
            All of your content and account data lives on
            <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">your own AudioSilo server</strong> and on
            <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">your own device</strong>, not with us.
          </li>
          <li>The app contacts only the server <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">you</strong> tell it to connect to.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2 class="mt-14 mb-4 font-display text-[1.625rem] font-bold tracking-[-0.03em]">What information the app handles</h2>
      <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-foreground/85">
        Because AudioSilo is self-hosted, almost everything stays between your device and the server
        you connect to.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6 mb-2 font-semibold text-foreground">Stored on your device</p>
      <ul class="mb-4 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-foreground/85 marker:text-subtle-foreground">
        <li>
          <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">Your session token</strong>, kept in the operating system's
          encrypted secure storage (Keychain on iOS, Keystore on Android) so you stay signed in.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">Downloaded audiobooks</strong>: audio files and cover art you
          choose to download for offline listening, stored in the app's private storage.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">App preferences</strong>: settings such as playback speed, theme,
          and language, plus a local cache of your listening position.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-6 mb-2 font-semibold text-foreground">Sent to the server you choose</p>
      <ul class="mb-4 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-foreground/85 marker:text-subtle-foreground">
        <li>
          When you sign in or pair, and as you listen, the app sends requests to the
          <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">AudioSilo server address you provide</strong>. Your account
          credentials, listening progress, bookmarks, notes, and favourites are stored on
          <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">that</strong> server, operated by you or your server's administrator.
        </li>
        <li>
          We (KodeStar) have <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">no access</strong> to your server, your account,
          or any data on it.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-foreground/85">
        There is no central AudioSilo account system. Your account exists only on your self-hosted
        server.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-14 mb-4 font-display text-[1.625rem] font-bold tracking-[-0.03em]">Device permissions</h2>
      <ul class="mb-4 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-foreground/85 marker:text-subtle-foreground">
        <li>
          <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">Camera</strong>: used solely to scan a pairing QR code when
          connecting to your server. Images are processed on-device to read the code and are never
          stored or transmitted to us.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">Background audio</strong>: so playback continues when the app is
          backgrounded or the screen is locked.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">Network access</strong>: to communicate with your AudioSilo server.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="mt-14 mb-4 font-display text-[1.625rem] font-bold tracking-[-0.03em]">Optional public demo</h2>
      <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-foreground/85">
        AudioSilo offers an optional, web-based public demo (at
        <span class="ic"
          >demo.audiosilo.app</span
        >) so people can try the player without setting up a server. The demo server creates a
        <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">temporary, throwaway guest session</strong> with sample content; no
        personal account is created and demo data is ephemeral. Using the demo is optional and separate
        from connecting to your own server.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-14 mb-4 font-display text-[1.625rem] font-bold tracking-[-0.03em]">Analytics, advertising, and tracking</h2>
      <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-foreground/85">
        AudioSilo contains <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">no</strong> analytics, advertising, attribution, or
        third-party tracking software. We do not profile you and do not build advertising identifiers.
        Nothing about your usage is reported back to us.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-14 mb-4 font-display text-[1.625rem] font-bold tracking-[-0.03em]">Third-party services</h2>
      <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-foreground/85">
        The app integrates no third-party data-collecting services. The only third parties involved
        are the <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">app stores</strong> (Apple App Store, Google Play) that
        distribute the app, and the <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">server you connect to</strong>, each
        governed by its own operator's terms.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-14 mb-4 font-display text-[1.625rem] font-bold tracking-[-0.03em]">Data retention and deletion</h2>
      <ul class="mb-4 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-foreground/85 marker:text-subtle-foreground">
        <li>
          <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">On your device:</strong> uninstalling the app removes its local
          data, including the stored session token, downloaded audiobooks, and preferences.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">On your server:</strong> your account and listening data are
          retained according to your server's configuration. Because the server is under your control,
          you can delete your account and its data there at any time.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="mt-14 mb-4 font-display text-[1.625rem] font-bold tracking-[-0.03em]">Children's privacy</h2>
      <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-foreground/85">
        AudioSilo is a general-audience audiobook player and is not directed at children under 13. We
        do not knowingly collect personal information from children; indeed, we collect personal
        information from no one.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-14 mb-4 font-display text-[1.625rem] font-bold tracking-[-0.03em]">Security</h2>
      <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-foreground/85">
        Communication between the app and your server uses standard transport security (HTTPS, which
        your server can be configured to enforce). Your session token is held in the device's
        encrypted secure storage. Because we hold no user data centrally, there is no central store of
        your information to be breached.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-14 mb-4 font-display text-[1.625rem] font-bold tracking-[-0.03em]">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-foreground/85">
        We may update this policy as the app evolves. Material changes will be reflected by the "Last
        updated" date above and published at the same URL.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-14 mb-4 font-display text-[1.625rem] font-bold tracking-[-0.03em]">Contact</h2>
      <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-foreground/85">
        Questions about this privacy policy can be sent to
        <a class={link} href="mailto:kode@audiosilo.app">kode@audiosilo.app</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
